  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "Single-DGX-Spark Qwen3.8-27B on Ash Hart's TensorFold engine v0.6.0 (exact decoding, custom CUDA kernels JIT-compiled on first start, stock upstream source) with Vontra's MLX 4-bit (group 64) checkpoint and z-lab's DFlash2 draft model, which TensorFold's CUDA engine requires unless drafting is switched off. One rank only: TensorFold's two-rank mode is not available here. Serves one request at a time by default (upstream CUDA default; the concurrency setting enables shared rounds) at the model's 262,144-token window. Image input (--vision) is an opt-in option that upstream still marks experimental. Upstream measured about 63 tok/s code and 46 tok/s chat with DFlash2 on a 64 GB M5 Pro and 46 to 50 tok/s on one DGX Spark (upstream claims, unmeasured here). Licences, for information: Qwen3.8-27B and the Vontra conversion are Apache-2.0; z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2 states Apache-2.0 on its model card (a mirror of incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2); TensorFold is Apache-2.0 from 0.6.0 (MIT up to 0.5.0). TensorFold v0.6.0 at c4646171139ee8a3c38103eaa1699dad226ec12b keeps every option this recipe passes; per upstream it adds bf16 CUDA prompt kernels by default, prompt fill inside decode rounds with concurrency above 1, resumed conversations, Prometheus /metrics and the opt-in --checkpoint-slots and --prefill-fp8 (not exposed here); the existing context bound, KV/drafting defaults, and one-stream resource profile are retained. The pinned ARM64 image includes xgrammar 0.2.8 and Apache TVM FFI 0.1.11 for OpenAI response_format structured-output requests.",
    "tags": [
      "dflash2",
      "engine",
      "image-input",
      "kernel-jit",
      "mlx-checkpoint",
      "qwen3.8",
      "reasoning",
      "spark",
      "speculative-decoding",
      "tensorfold"
    ],
    "title": "Qwen3.8 27B TensorFold single Spark"
  },
